    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43688" root="&#xA;                        ملق&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            5
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَلَّقَهُ</span></b> 
                        , (S, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَلَّقَ لَهُ</span>, (S, Msb, K,)
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَلُّقٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِمِلَّاقٌ</span>, [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِحِمَّالٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِكِلَّامٌ</span>,
not <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمْلَاقٌ</span> as in the CK,] <i>He behaved in a
loving,</i> or <i>an affectionate, and a blandishing,</i> or
<i>coaxing, manner to him.</i> (S, Msb, * K.) See a
verse cited in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رضو</span>, conj. 5.

